<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-pseudoobscura-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila pseudoobscura Turing wavelength at 2.0 µm (detail rung, 0 Ma) — Code-to-model traceability: 88/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The module docstring writes h(k²) and k_c², and growth_rate, classic_kc2, and the Lean theorems are the same statements. The chronoseries block records Δlog10 = -2.003 versus planitibia and +1.717 versus santomea at Δage = 0. The linear horizon is labelled as Pass 1, not as a steady PDE." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-pseudoobscura-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-pseudoobscura-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-pseudoobscura-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila pseudoobscura Turing wavelength at 2.0 µm (detail rung, 0 Ma) — Model fidelity to source: 84/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "growth_rate implements the largest real eigenvalue of J - k² D, and classic_kc2 is the minimizer (D_v f_u + D_u g_v) / (2 D_u D_v). The fastest mode is 1.961 µm and the classic k_c wavelength is 1.946 µm, the shift expected just above onset. simulate_field then amplifies noise for a fixed six e-folds. There is no saturating nonlinearity, so the late-time amplitude is not a steady state of a nonlinear PDE." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-pseudoobscura-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-pseudoobscura-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-pseudoobscura-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.4e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-pseudoobscura-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila pseudoobscura Turing wavelength at 2.0 µm (detail rung, 0 Ma) — Morphometric validation: 86/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The spectral centroid is 1.9569 µm against the assigned 1.961 µm. The diffusivity sweep has Pearson r = 0.99988, RMSE = 0.0071 µm, and KS = 0.0625 (not zero). The specimen mask gives foreground fraction 0.140 (reference 0.45), circularity 0.105 (reference 1, a round ocellus), and coherency 0.652 (reference 0.32). These references are not copies of the measurements. Peak-to-peak spacing on the 2D field is not yet measured, and 1.961 µm is an assigned rung rather than a wet-lab period." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-pseudoobscura-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-chronoseries-delta-log10-vs-planitibia>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-pseudoobscura-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-equal-diffusion-sigma-max-per-s>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-pseudoobscura-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-fastest-mode-wavelength-um>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-pseudoobscura-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-specimen-contour-circularity>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-pseudoobscura-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-specimen-foreground-fraction>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-pseudoobscura-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-specimen-structure-tensor-coherency>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-pseudoobscura-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-stripe-wavelength-centroid-um>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-pseudoobscura-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-wavelength-sweep-ks-statistic>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-pseudoobscura-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-wavelength-sweep-pearson-r>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-pseudoobscura-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-wavelength-sweep-rmse-um>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-pseudoobscura-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-pseudoobscura-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.6e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-pseudoobscura-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila pseudoobscura Turing wavelength at 2.0 µm (detail rung, 0 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 86.1/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 1 selects a 1.961 µm wavelength from the Turing dispersion relation just above onset and compares that rung with the planitibia 197.2 µm and santomea 102 µm primordium neighbours, all at 0 Ma. The linear field, diffusivity sweep (Pearson r = 0.99988), and equal-diffusion ablation are rendered beside the CC BY-SA male. A cubic steady state, peak-to-peak spacing, and a drawn specimen mask are still open. Overall 86.1/100 (faithfulness 84.6, reproducibility 89.8); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.18.1, pillow 13.0.0, matplotlib 3.11.2. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 84, Morphological realism / specimen match 82, Parameter expressivity 90, Morphometric validation 86, Source and data traceability 91, Code-to-model traceability 88, Reproducibility package 90. Output judged: docs/media/drosophila_pseudoobscura_turing_wavelength_s0_growth.gif: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-pseudoobscura-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d, image/gif, 859649 B, 640×480 px, 12 frames, artifact_sha256 39e4d8da093929fba50e19cf54ba06ee268ec8555e9ccb5cae777ae9110b5c78 (sha256 39e4d8da093929fba50e19cf54ba06ee268ec8555e9ccb5cae777ae9110b5c78), spec_fingerprint 965c9feaa244c1d56d6c4a07371f6ea2f5478ae5cc72e76fe09fa1a3b7eec04c. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 965c9feaa244c1d56d6c4a07371f6ea2f5478ae5cc72e76fe09fa1a3b7eec04c; artifact_sha256: 39e4d8da093929fba50e19cf54ba06ee268ec8555e9ccb5cae777ae9110b5c78; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/drosophila_pseudoobscura_turing_wavelength_s0/drosophila_pseudoobscura_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=19f8aa499fe6bbdd..., datasets/drosophila_pseudoobscura_turing_wavelength_s0/drosophila_pseudoobscura_turing_wavelength_s0_specimen.jpg=8bb7f34ac600cac7..., datasets/drosophila_pseudoobscura_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=ff6dbcfc60370723..., datasets/drosophila_pseudoobscura_turing_wavelength_s0/scout_manifest.json=4cf8077a656a0c44...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing (1952) gives the two-species dispersion relation and the conditions for a diffusion-driven band. | Richards et al. (2005) sequenced D. pseudoobscura and describe its chromosomal evolution. They do not report a Turing wavelength. | Kopp (2011) reviews sex-comb evolution. The two-segment comb is not a 1.961 µm stripe. | The Hanson 2019 Commons file is a lateral photograph of an adult male under CC BY-SA 4.0.; reconstructed_in_script: Jacobian (0.84, -0.90, 1.55, -1.20) s^-1 and diffusivities D_u = 0.028046, D_v = 0.131825 µm²/s place the fastest mode at 1.961 µm. | Fourier integration of broadband noise for six e-folds, a diffusivity-scale sweep, and an equal-diffusion ablation. | Chronoseries comparison: Δlog10 λ versus planitibia is -2.003 and versus santomea is +1.717, with Δage = 0 Ma.; transfer_boundary: 1.961e-6 m is the assigned detail rung of this slot, not a published histological period for a D. pseudoobscura ocellus or pigment granule. | Planitibia and santomea wavelengths are the primordium rungs of neighbouring MorphoEval slots, not measurements made in this script.; does_not_claim: That Richards 2005 measured a reaction-diffusion wavelength. | That the sex comb or the third-chromosome inversions are produced by this 2 µm mode. | That planitibia → pseudoobscura → santomea is a stratigraphic ancestor-descendant series. | That the growth GIF is a time-lapse of embryogenesis. It is a linear mode growing under the adult habitus.." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "open need [model_equation/model-fidelity, pressure P=3.4]: Replace the fixed six-e-fold linear horizon with a cubic saturation so the activator reaches a bounded amplitude.",
        "open need [morphometric_validation/morphometric-validation, pressure P=2.75]: Measure peak-to-peak spacing on the 2D field and compare it to 1.961 µm. The present KS is only between analytic and discrete dispersion samples.",
        "open need [specimen_comparison/specimen-match, pressure P=1.7]: Draw the specimen foreground mask on the comparison figure. Circularity and coherency are computed but not shown.",
        "remediation needed: Add a cubic saturation so the activator amplitude is a bounded steady state rather than a fixed six-e-fold horizon.",
        "remediation needed: Draw the specimen foreground mask on the comparison figure.",
        "remediation needed: Measure peak-to-peak spacing on the 2D field and test it against 1.961 µm. The present KS compares only analytic and discrete dispersion samples.",
        "remediation needed: Show the 2 µm field at a readable scale in the growth animation without dropping last-frame CV similarity below 58." ;
    pk:hasScore 8.61e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-pseudoobscura-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila pseudoobscura Turing wavelength at 2.0 µm (detail rung, 0 Ma) — Parameter expressivity: 90/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Scaling both diffusivities by s² scales λ_* by s and leaves σ_* unchanged. Across s in [0.70, 1.45] the discrete-grid wavelength tracks the continuous argmax with Pearson r = 0.99988 and RMSE = 0.0071 µm. Panel E of the comparison figure shows that monotonic control. The equal-diffusion ablation drops max σ from +0.0073 s⁻¹ to -0.18 s⁻¹." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-pseudoobscura-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-pseudoobscura-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 9e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

