    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-pseudoobscura-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/drosophila_pseudoobscura_turing_wavelength_s0_growth.gif; organism: Drosophila pseudoobscura; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.18.1, pillow 13.0.0, matplotlib 3.11.2; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing (1952) gives the two-species dispersion relation and the conditions for a diffusion-driven band. | Richards et al. (2005) sequenced D. pseudoobscura and describe its chromosomal evolution. They do not report a Turing wavelength. | Kopp (2011) reviews sex-comb evolution. The two-segment comb is not a 1.961 µm stripe. | The Hanson 2019 Commons file is a lateral photograph of an adult male under CC BY-SA 4.0.; reconstructed_in_script: Jacobian (0.84, -0.90, 1.55, -1.20) s^-1 and diffusivities D_u = 0.028046, D_v = 0.131825 µm²/s place the fastest mode at 1.961 µm. | Fourier integration of broadband noise for six e-folds, a diffusivity-scale sweep, and an equal-diffusion ablation. | Chronoseries comparison: Δlog10 λ versus planitibia is -2.003 and versus santomea is +1.717, with Δage = 0 Ma.; transfer_boundary: 1.961e-6 m is the assigned detail rung of this slot, not a published histological period for a D. pseudoobscura ocellus or pigment granule. | Planitibia and santomea wavelengths are the primordium rungs of neighbouring MorphoEval slots, not measurements made in this script.; does_not_claim: That Richards 2005 measured a reaction-diffusion wavelength. | That the sex comb or the third-chromosome inversions are produced by this 2 µm mode. | That planitibia → pseudoobscura → santomea is a stratigraphic ancestor-descendant series. | That the growth GIF is a time-lapse of embryogenesis. It is a linear mode growing under the adult habitus.]; other sources: Drosophila pseudoobscura male (File:Dpse_1.tif) <https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dpse_1.tif>; phenomenon_size: 1.9 µm (1.919e-06 m, log10=-5.717 m, tier=3_subcellular_um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 1.9 µm to 4.3 mm): 1.9 µm:drosophila-affinis-bioelectric-polarity, 6.0 µm:drosophila-affinis-vertex-packing, 96 µm:drosophila-affinis-turing-wavelength, 192 µm:drosophila-affinis-clock-wavefront, 432 µm:drosophila-affinis-morphogen-condensation, 528 µm:drosophila-affinis-elastic-buckling, 600 µm:drosophila-affinis-flux-canalization, 840 µm:drosophila-affinis-branching-tree" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1952.0012>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1101/gr.3059305>,
